# F5-style single source: the verification-command vocabulary shared by the
# bash engine (phase-graph.sh sources this file) and the console's runner
# (viewer/server/runner/verify-env.ts parses the same file). Change a list
# only here — a drift test on the viewer side pins the two readers together.
#
# NOT here on purpose: the runner's read-only command allowlist (VERBS /
# REACHES_OUT in viewer/server/runner/verify.ts). Those carry per-verb
# judgement — closures over subcommands and flags — and flattening them into
# an env line would fake a single source while hiding the half that matters.

# Leads whose meaning depends on the working directory. A §Verification
# command that starts with one of these and declares no **Verify in:** runs
# at the repository root, where it may test the wrong tree (lint F18 warns at
# plan time; the runner's boarding preflight warns again at run time).
CWD_SENSITIVE="docker docker-compose pnpm npm yarn task make just pytest go cargo alembic vitest jest tsc node"

# Names never worth a resolution warning: shell builtins, keywords and
# always-present tools. Lint F17 and the runner's boarding preflight both
# skip them. The keywords matter for the runner's file probe — `if` and `do`
# are not files on any PATH and must not read as "missing binaries".
PREFLIGHT_SKIP="cd true false echo printf test pwd env which bash sh command export set time if then fi elif else for while until do done case esac"
